more pleasing to him. The King of Poland loved it. And so it turned out later, did the Communist. They liked Palotto's paintings because they showed a full range of society, not just the elite. They also liked his paintings because they were of the city before the heyday of capitalism, when Warsaw, as they saw it, was still pure. In fact, there was plenty of other documentation of Warsaw's historic section. A group of architects and students did painstaking work during the war before the destruction, creating blueprints, taking photographs. And a lot of those blueprints were used in the Warsaw reconstruction.
更合他的心意。波兰国王对此喜爱有加。事实证明，后来共产主义者也同样喜欢。他们喜欢贝洛托的画作，因为这些画作展现了社会的各个阶层，而不仅仅是精英。他们还喜欢他的画作，因为这些画作描绘的是资本主义鼎盛时期之前的城市，在他们看来，那时的华沙依然是纯净的。事实上，关于华沙历史街区的文献还有很多。一群建筑师和学生在战争爆发前的毁灭前夕进行了艰苦卓绝的工作，绘制了蓝图，拍摄了照片。其中的许多蓝图都被用于华沙的重建。

